# TypeScript AI Agent Framework with Suspend/Resume Workflows
created: 2025-06-26, last updated: 2026-04-25, [Read more](https://www.codeline.co/thoughts/repo-review/2025/voltagent-typescript-ai-agent-framework-with-workflows-and-observability)

That's what makes the console's trace view show the full agent hierarchy rather than a flat log.
The workflow engine is in `packages/core/src/workflow/`.
`createWorkflowChain` returns a `WorkflowChain` class with a fluent builder API — `.andThen()`, `.andWhen()`, `.andAgent()`, `.andMap()`, `.andRace()`, `.andSleep()`, and more.
Each step receives `{ data, suspend, resumeData }`.
The suspend mechanism in `suspend-controller.ts` wraps the native `AbortController`:
```
export function createSuspendController(): WorkflowSuspendController {
const abortController = new AbortController();
let suspensionReason: string | undefined;
let suspended = false;
return {
signal: abortController.signal,
suspend: (reason?: string) => {
if (!suspended && !cancelled) {
suspensionReason = reason;
suspended = true;
abortController.abort({ type: "suspended", reason });
}
},
isSuspended: () => suspended,
getReason: () => suspensionReason,
// ...
};
}
```

